 "poem": "But I am our Lord, our,\nOur God above the heavens,\nSoul of all who sinned or sat beneath,\nWho created and made us man before.\nYou have come to me because\nI knew not that you alone\nAnd you are my friend, but thou hast spoken\nThat I was in hell's deep depths before.\nOh soul! thy feet came out again\nFrom the world where thou hadst wandered,\nWhat a splendid sight is this earth again,\nWith such a heaven as heaven before.",
